    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d360">

                <pb facs="0512" n="254" xml:id="pg254"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 165.102/511</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-05-10T13:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 10, 1915, 1 p.m</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 11, 3.30 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2199. Department’s 1629, 5th. Foreign Office inquires preliminarily whether <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Neches</hi> brings cargo destined for Germany, what such
                    cargo is composed of, and whether its transshipment through Holland is
                    guaranteed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
